The $"Geo"(p)$ distribution on $Omega = NN$ models the number of Bernoulli trials needed to get the first success:
$
  p_k = (1 - p)^(k - 1) p quad forall k in NN.
$
For example, it models tosses of a biased coin with heads probability $p$ up to the first heads; the probabilities sum to $1$ as a geometric series.
